vivaQuestions: [
{ question: "What is the purpose of studying Cloud Case-Studies?", answer: "Sir, it helps us understand practical implementations, overview of real-world cloud services, and how businesses solve problems using cloud architecture." },
{ question: "What is involved in Designing Solutions for the Cloud?", answer: "It involves analyzing requirements, selecting the right service model (IaaS/PaaS/SaaS), planning for scalability, and ensuring security architecture." },
{ question: "What does it mean to Implement & Integrate Solutions?", answer: "It is the practical deployment of designed cloud solutions and connecting them seamlessly with existing legacy systems or other cloud services." },
{ question: "How is the Cloud impacting Emerging Markets?", answer: "It lowers the barrier to entry for startups in emerging markets by eliminating huge upfront hardware costs, allowing them to scale globally." },
{ question: "What is Eucalyptus used for in building a Private Cloud?", answer: "Eucalyptus is used to deploy Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) on local hardware, creating an AWS-compatible private cloud." },
{ question: "What is AppScale?", answer: "AppScale is an open-source platform that allows users to deploy and host their own Platform as a Service (PaaS), often running on top of IaaS." },
{ question: "How does AppScale integrate with Eucalyptus?", answer: "According to the syllabus, AppScale (PaaS) can be deployed on top of Eucalyptus (IaaS) to create a full cloud stack on private infrastructure." },
{ question: "What is a major benefit of using AppScale?", answer: "It provides an API compatible with Google App Engine, allowing developers to run GAE apps on their own private infrastructure without lock-in." },
{ question: "What is the importance of IaaS in a private cloud setup?", answer: "IaaS abstracts the physical hardware, providing the fundamental virtual machines and networking required to build higher-level services." },
{ question: "Give an example of a cloud solution for an emerging market.", answer: "Mobile banking or micro-finance applications hosted on scalable public clouds to serve rural populations securely and cheaply." },
{ question: "What is a 'lift and shift' cloud migration?", answer: "It is a strategy where an application and its data are moved to the cloud with minimal or no redesign." },
{ question: "What is a cloud-native application?", answer: "An application specifically designed and built to run optimally in the cloud, utilizing microservices and containerization." },
{ question: "Why integrate legacy systems with the cloud?", answer: "To leverage the scalability of the cloud while retaining critical, hard-to-replace on-premise databases and business logic." },
{ question: "What is the role of APIs in cloud integration?", answer: "APIs act as the communication bridge allowing different cloud services and on-premise software to exchange data." },
{ question: "What challenge do emerging markets face with cloud adoption?", answer: "Challenges include unreliable internet connectivity, lack of local data centers, and data sovereignty laws." },
{ question: "How does Eucalyptus provide AWS compatibility?", answer: "It translates AWS API calls into its own internal format, allowing tools built for AWS EC2/S3 to work on Eucalyptus." },
{ question: "What is PaaS on IaaS?", answer: "It is layering a development platform (PaaS like AppScale) over virtualized infrastructure (IaaS like Eucalyptus) for maximum control." },
{ question: "What is serverless computing in cloud solutions?", answer: "A design where the cloud provider dynamically manages the allocation and provisioning of servers, and the user only writes code (Functions)." },
{ question: "How do case studies help in choosing a cloud player?", answer: "They highlight the strengths and limitations of different providers in real-world scenarios, aiding in strategic decision-making." },
{ question: "What is hybrid cloud integration?", answer: "Connecting an organization's on-premise private cloud securely with a public cloud provider to share data and workloads." }
],
